# Unambiguous names

A basename must identify the concept **without opening the file**. This applies
to `src/`, `tests/`, `docs/`, `.cursor/`, and host packages — not only tests.

## Rules

- Prefer the **domain term** over a short generic noun when both exist in this
  codebase (`JudgementPolicy` → `judgement_policy`, not `policy`).
- Mirror source ↔ test: `judgement_policy.py` ↔ `test_judgement_policy.py`.
- One concern per test module. Do not dump unrelated areas into a bag file
  (`test_phases.py`).
- If two peers could share a short name (`policy` vs `AccessPolicy`,
  `connection` vs HTTP vs DB), pick the longer disambiguator at the leaf.
- Deprecate public imports with a thin re-export shim; update call sites and
  docs in the same change when practical.

## Litmus

From `ls tests/` or `ls src/mechaharness/`, would a newcomer pick the right
file for the concept they have in mind? If not, rename before merge.

```text
# BAD — ambiguous in a listing
policy.py / test_policy.py
decisions.py / operations.py / connection.py
test_phases.py          # graph + routing + research + …

# GOOD — domain-clear at the leaf
judgement_policy.py / test_judgement_policy.py
decision_log.py / operation_registry.py / api_connection.py
test_graph.py, test_routing.py, test_research.py, …
```

`AccessPolicy` stays under access-oriented names (`access`, `test_access`); do
not reuse bare `policy` for judgement verdicts.
